course: dictionary
lesson: 5338
title: The Khanty people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Khanty is a name for a people, and a name for their language. The Khanty are an Indigenous people who live in western Siberia, in Russia, near the Ob River. In «Siberian peoples such as the Khanty, Evenks and Yakuts lost land, and many died from new diseases and violence», the words «such as» tell you that the Khanty are one example from a list of peoples.
explain: Look for clues in the words around a name. The capital letter at the start shows that Khanty is a name, not an ordinary word. Words like «peoples» and «Siberian» tell you the Khanty belong to the peoples of the far north.
explain: Some words can be used in more than one way. Khanty can be a noun for the people (the Khanty), or it can describe something that belongs to them. Their language is also called Khanty, and it is related to Hungarian.
fact: The Khanty are an Indigenous people of western Siberia, in Russia.
fact: They live near the Ob River.
fact: Many Khanty traditionally herd reindeer, fish and hunt.
fact: Khanty is also the name of their language, which is related to Hungarian.
fact: Their land is in the Khanty-Mansi region of Russia.
exercise: Who are the Khanty? | A river in Hungary | A type of reindeer | *An Indigenous people who live in western Siberia, in Russia | A famous Russian writer
exercise: Khanty is also the name of a language. Which language is it related to? | *Hungarian | Japanese | English | Spanish
exercise: Many Khanty traditionally herd which animal? | *Reindeer | Penguins | Lions | Camels
test: Near which river do the Khanty live? | Nile | Thames | *Ob | Amazon
test: Where is the Khanty-Mansi region? | In Canada's far north | In Hungary | In Mongolia | *In Russia
exam: What happened to Siberian peoples such as the Khanty, according to «Siberian peoples such as the Khanty, Evenks and Yakuts lost land, and many died from new diseases and violence»? | They moved into big cities | They became rich from fishing | They were given more land and more reindeer | *They lost land, and many died from new diseases and violence
